    {
      "id": "OGA-04",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-geometric-local-tests",
      "title": "Generic products and a reverse injection recover the local data at a specified prime",
      "hypotheses": "The rank-m extracted representation and both inclusions are available for every eligible geometric piece. A piece realizing each prescribed local comparison exists. The multiplicative genericity polynomial does not vanish where exact Satake or Weil polynomials are required. The coefficient-prime target is spherical and outside the two auxiliary real-subfield fibres.",
      "statement": "Away from ℓ the determinant fixes the multiplicities of the roots of the annihilator. Above ℓ the injection into the crystalline piece gives crystallinity; its injection back into copies of the target forces all m distinct jumps to occur there. The same product test fixes a degree minus one Weil polynomial and unramifiedness gives the other degrees. Orienting the auxiliary primes preserves their real-subfield fibres.",
